    {
      "id": "wikipedia-article-source-contract",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Article Source Contract",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -560,
        "y": -80
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 380,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Wikipedia Article Source\n\nThe root resolves only enough data to browse spatially: canonical URL, title, revision/source identity, attribution, lead content, the first useful section, and a section manifest.\n\nEach section manifest entry must provide a stable `id`, visible `title`, `level`, `order`, and source locator. Runtime presentation derives one labeled expansion handle per section. Section bodies are resolved lazily after expansion.\n\nLarge section counts are a presentation problem, not a reason to weaken the source contract.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "wikipedia-article-source-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
